# Violin
# Scales — 3-octave modes with fingerings from modeShifts
Roots: [roots=keys()]

# The per-mode card mirrors the original Scales3Oct contents: `[key] [mode]
# [fingering]`, with mode and fingering in separate tags. modeFingering draws
# from the same distribution as before (shifts + shiftStrings over
# `0112223333`), but the shift count now comes from modeShifts(root) so it
# matches each mode's actual 3-octave climb.
-=- scale-mode
Scales3Oct: [key] [modeName(mode)]mode [modeFingering(key, mode)]fingering

# One subdeck, `scales`. The {} spawns one card per mode of each root: each
# iteration fixes `mode`, re-evaluates the scale-mode block, and the resulting
# lines land in the subdeck as new cards.
-=- scales::
{roots.flatMap(k => { key = k; return modeShifts(key).flatMap((_, m) => { mode = m; return blockLines('scale-mode') \}) \})}
